Swizzle view expressions are enabled by the [=language_extension/swizzle_assignment=] language extension.

A [=swizzle view=] is formed by:
* Applying a multi-letter [=swizzle=] name to a [=reference type|reference=] or [=pointer type|pointer=] value
    with [=access/read_write=] access mode and whose [=store type=] is a vector, or
* Applying a multi-letter [=swizzle=] name to a swizzle view.

By these rules, the index list part of a swizzle view is fully determined at
[=shader module creation|shader-creation=] time.

In this section the <dfn noexport>swizzle index function</dfn> SI is defined as:
* SI(`x`) &equals; 0
* SI(`y`) &equals; 1
* SI(`z`) &equals; 2
* SI(`w`) &equals; 3
* SI(`r`) &equals; 0
* SI(`g`) &equals; 1
* SI(`b`) &equals; 2
* SI(`a`) &equals; 3

We say a <dfn noexport>[=swizzle=] name |Z| represents the |K| indices &laquo;&nbsp;|Idx|<sub>0</sub>, ..., |Idx|<sub>|K|&minus;1</sub> &raquo;</dfn> if:

* One of the following is true:
    * Each letter in |Z| is `x`, `y`, `z`, or `w`, or
    * Each letter in |Z| is `r`, `g`, `b`, or `a`
* Each |Idx|<sub>|i|</sub> equals SI(|L|), where |L| is the |i|'th letter in |Z|.

Note: For example, the swizzle `wzyx` represents the four indices &laquo;3, 2,
1, 0&raquo;, and the swizzle `rb` represents the two indices &laquo;0, 2&raquo;.
The swizzle `rgbz` does not represent any index sequence, since it mixes `rgba`
and `xyzw` letters.

